<Base title="webE" description="The webE specification, how to build apps and sites on webE, and how to extend khensu.nu through code and consensus.">
  <p class="eyebrow">webE · specification</p>
  <h1>webE: a new network, alongside the internet</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    webE is an open protocol for names without DNS, content without CDNs, websites, feeds, forums and live media, all
    delivered over a post-quantum stealth network. Nodes only relay, cache and count; encoding, encryption, ranking,
    moderation and rendering happen on devices. khensu.nu is the first webE app. Anyone can build another.
  </p>

  <h2 id="spec">Specification</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Transport</td><td>Outfox mix network with ML-KEM-1024, constant stealth ticks, two-relay MOQ paths over padded trunks, all carried as ordinary HTTPS</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Names</td><td><code>name.khensu.nu</code>, resolved from the key transparency log through private lookups, never from DNS or certificate authorities</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Objects</td><td>Content-addressed chunks, signed site manifests and roots, erasure-coded across operators</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Fetch and publish</td><td>Two-relay stealth fetch; publishing through the ticks or the owner’s node, never as a visible burst</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Applications</td><td>Sites, feeds, forums, labels and live tracks</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Clients</td><td>The khensu.nu app’s viewer for <code>webe://</code>, a Chromium extension, then a Chromium patch</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The full documents, in <code>khensu-specs</code>:</p>
